  "summary": "Harold Vance (pt-0002) has been reviewed against RBC-PHARM-07. Only one medicine needed a change, gabapentin, which I reduced. His apixaban and metformin stay the same.\n\n**Values used:**\n- **Age:** 82.\n- **Creatinine:** 1.21 mg/dL on 10/20. I skipped the 1.88 from 10/21 because it's marked entered-in-error (the specimen was mislabelled and belongs to another patient).\n- **Weight:** 64.9 kg (143 lb), measured 10/20. I skipped the 132 lb from 10/22 because it was his guess by phone, not a weighing.\n- **Kidney function:** eGFR 59.8 (CKD-EPI 2021) and CrCl 43.2 mL/min (Cockcroft-Gault).\n\n**Results by medicine:**\n- **Apixaban 2.5 mg twice daily:** no change. The policy's apixaban section only covers atrial fibrillation. He takes it long-term to prevent another clot after his August 2025 PE. St. Brigid hematology set this dose and said it isn't a kidney-adjusted dose, and his chart has no atrial fibrillation. Even if that section did apply, he meets only one of its criteria (age).\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily:** no change, since his eGFR is above 45.\n- **Gabapentin:** his dose was 600 mg three times daily (1800 mg/day), above the policy's 400–1400 mg/day range for his kidney function. I changed the existing order to 600 mg twice daily (1200 mg/day). That uses the same tablet and stays near the top of the range to keep his nerve pain controlled. The new order is mr-t0001.\n- **His other medicines:** the policy doesn't cover them, so I left them alone.\n\nPharmacy's 10/21 suggestions (lower metformin, gabapentin 300 mg once daily) were based on the creatinine that was entered in error, which is why I didn't follow them.\n\n**Done:**\n- Signed your progress note with the values, each result and the change, with sources cited (doc-t0002).\n- Messaged the pharmacist, Grace Lindqvist, explaining why my results differ from her screen.\n- Messaged Mr. Vance about the new gabapentin dose. I told him to keep his other medicines the same and to call if his pain comes back or he feels drowsy or unsteady.",
